{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread","id":625380,"title":"What do US (and non-US) citizens think about this guy? [Politics thread]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T06:32:17-07:00","id":625380,"title":"What do US (and non-US) citizens think about this guy? [Politics thread]","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C7L9V7oGRv8\" data-code=\"C7L9V7oGRv8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/C7L9V7oGRv8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> As a European and a graduate of politics, I must say that the Bernie Sanders campaign has caught me by surprise. Is this for real? Is he honestly leading the poll for the Democrat presidential candidacy? What do American forum members think of him?<br /> <br /> (I ask this because my initial reaction to this guy is very positive)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 08-13-2015, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:31:42-07:00","id":625625,"title":"","content":"In b4 a random sniper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:53:09-07:00","id":625636,"title":"","content":"Last I checked he wasn't leading the democratic candidates polls but that he was climbing fairly quickly. <br /> <br /> I agree with most of his history and polices, some I disagree with. I'm living in the US but don't get a vote (being a foreigner and all), but barring something new I'd encourage voting for 'em. I don't know if in the unlikely event he becomes the democratic representative and in the more unlikely event he were to win that he'd be able to accomplish all that much, but step in the right direction and all that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T10:15:54-07:00","id":625672,"title":"","content":"Bernie's certainly a real candidate. He's the only current serious contender to HRC; the rest of the Democratic Party candidates really don't have enough driving force.<br /> <br /> He's also ahead in <b>one</b> poll in New Hampshire. Which basically means squat (almost all the polls at this point basically mean squat outside of the weird thing the RNC is doing with their debates to handle their massive 17 candidate field), because it's a single poll, in a single state (favorable to Bernie in general), ages before anyone votes on anything. Keep in mind the first time New Hampshire voters will cast a ballot on this is in February.<br /> <br /> There's actually a fairly significant backlash amongst the US polling organizations at how poorly the US media is using the polling data. Polling at this point in US presidential races is almost universally insignificant. It's just laying the foundations for a solid polling data set in a few months.<br /> <br /> I like Bernie, though I'm not sure he's the best choice from a general election perspective. The current state of things leaves the Democrats with a huge electoral advantage, but that means a candidate that can pull swing states is all the more important. The real test for Bernie's viability isn't Iowa and New Hampshire, it's places like Ohio and Virginia. Because those are the states that are actually going to decide the election in the end (in terms of statistical uncertainty).<br /> <br /> That said, I think Bernie's actually a lot like Biden: a really good Vice President in the making. He's extremely experienced in DC and really does know how to make the system work. He'd be a hell of an operative for pushing the general liberal/progressive Democratic platform in the Congress.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:58:26-07:00","id":625765,"title":"","content":"I intend to vote for him. I agree with most of what he says, and I disapprove of putting another goddamned political dynasty into office.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T14:49:31-07:00","id":625952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=625765#post625765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I intend to vote for him. I agree with most of what he says, and I disapprove of putting another goddamned political dynasty into office.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What Jim said, only replace &quot;I intend to&quot; with &quot;I'm gunna&quot;, &quot;I disapprove of&quot; with &quot;I'm sure as hell not&quot; and &quot;goddamned&quot; with &quot;motherfucking&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T16:11:03-07:00","id":626028,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I forgot to mention I am still shocked no legal action was brought against Secretary Clinton for her destruction of those e-mails. Those e-mails were the property of the people, and what she did is no different from walking into a records room and torching a box of papers while saying no, it's okay, those records totally didn't have anything important on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T18:05:30-07:00","id":626088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626028#post626028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I forgot to mention I am still shocked no legal action was brought against Secretary Clinton for her destruction of those e-mails. Those e-mails were the property of the people, and what she did is no different from walking into a records room and torching a box of papers while saying no, it's okay, those records totally didn't have anything important on them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> character limits rdyojtddsgjudk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T22:35:43-07:00","id":626342,"title":"","content":"Well... I guess talking about Bernie wasn't destined to last long.<br /> <br /> It does speak kind of poorly for him when the loudest things are not, &quot;Here's why Bernie's awesome,&quot; but rather, &quot;Here's why I'm not voting for Hillary.&quot;<br /> <br /> Though I never did get the whole, &quot;dynasty,&quot; thing. It's a democracy. We should select people based on their merits, not their family. Which also means, &quot;they're related to a past president,&quot; shouldn't matter either. FDR was related to eleven past presidents. Good thing nobody held that against him... And exceedingly few presidents didn't come from political families; even if that didn't mean a lot of presidents per family.<br /> <br /> The e-mails are also a pretty much non-scandal. You know what happens to the vast majority of such things? They get deleted, either on purpose, or by neglect, because the government generates a vast amount of records, and doesn't employ nearly enough archivists to actually do anything with them. So most of them get dumped somewhere, and never get found because nobody actually cares about them.<br /> <br /> Even if deleting them would be something that you could consider a crime... bringing legal action does... nothing. Because there's no case. Innocent until proven guilty remember? How do you prove she deleted something she shouldn't have, instead of something she was within her rights to delete... if she deleted them thoroughly enough that they can't be recovered (and if they could be recovered, they could be turned over...). It was certainly a stupid thing for her to do, but if she committed a crime in doing it there's no way to prove it. So bringing charges is just a waste of time and money because there's no case to build in an actual court. As such, it's only valuable as a political attack against her in the court of public opinion where suspicious is all you need compared to actual proof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T03:37:14-07:00","id":626473,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your replies. Yeah, I found out it's just one poll, but nonetheless, this guy looks....genuine. If, by some benevolent twist of history, he ends up as the Democratic candidate (or better yet, the POTUS), the US will have returned to the good old times when it was more progressive and radical than its European cousins. That is, if Bernie is allowed to implement his policies.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms: Your argument makes sense, and Sanders himself wants to keep his campaign on a positive note. That said, Clinton scares me in a TTIP-TPP-TISA signing kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T05:14:48-07:00","id":626494,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with Heavy Arms, though I appreciate the sentiment. I know it goes pretty much directly against Sanders' warning not to give into despair, but more than good intentions are needed to be an effective president. You need to be able to make those good intentions manifest without the rest of the government standing in your way. It's a cynical view but I'd be concerned about his ability to get stuff done.<br /> <br /> Time will tell, once we're further on the road to a new president. I get the feeling the next president will be Republican, if they get their shit together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:24:32-07:00","id":626662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626494#post626494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time will tell, once we're further on the road to a new president. I get the feeling the next president will be Republican, if they get their shit together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still think that Trump is there to poison the well as it where.<br /> <br /> US politics has been using dog whistles for a while, it's somewhat nice to see someone just kick the can and speak to the party voters directly about it as it sinks the party. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T09:57:19-07:00","id":626719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626342#post626342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I never did get the whole, &quot;dynasty,&quot; thing. It's a democracy. We should select people based on their merits, not their family. Which also means, &quot;they're related to a past president,&quot; shouldn't matter either. FDR was related to eleven past presidents. Good thing nobody held that against him... And exceedingly few presidents didn't come from political families; even if that didn't mean a lot of presidents per family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where I see the bigger headache coming in is fame and association with fame.<br /> <br /> People hear a name, recognise it, it fits into some shapes in their mind, and the contexts associated with that shape decide level of support. This is why actors have a major leg up, people know &quot;Oh hey he's that famous actor guy that does action movies or was it cowboy movies?&quot;. This is why presidents have a significant advantage in second term elections. This is why people link families together. You are supporting a Bush, so he's probably going to be like that previous Bush and the Bush before him, or you're supporting a Kennedy, well he'll probably be like the other bits of the Kennedy family elected.<br /> <br /> It's one of those fuzzy lines for the US... there are a lot of powerful, rich, political families. They have all the advantages that increase the odds of them getting elected if they go into politics. They have reasons to go into politics. And that makes some people uncomfortable since your leaders coming from largely family lines... well, it's that whole US and kings and lords thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:08:27-07:00","id":626722,"title":"","content":"As a sort of semi-follow on, and loop back politicians always need to appeal to the drama of the day. If they don't they tend to get not elected*, BS is doing exactly that right now. Congress, and the government itself has been hitting all-time lows for popularity, they've been fighting over measures that people on one side or another support, they've been through a very rough economic situation and while it's getting better, the buying power of the majority of americans is lower now than when a minimum wage was introduced. Combined with the media focus on the very long existing issue of racism and militarization of the police force, all things that BS has spent decades opposing (be it because it's his personal view or simply to have an established brand). He is portraying himself as a reasonable man of the people that puts the working man FIRST, and is the direct reverse of the presentation of most of washington. This is exactly the pitch that resonates with the populace right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> *-My opponent voted against adding security requirements to credit card data after the mass theft incident, *I* support such things because unlike my opponent *I* am not in the pocket of big credit card companies dancing to whatever they want!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T10:44:57-07:00","id":626736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626342#post626342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... I guess talking about Bernie wasn't destined to last long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just wanted to remind people that destruction of public records happened. I think people have forgotten.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:44:02-07:00","id":626829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626736#post626736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to remind people that destruction of public records happened. I think people have forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so much a question of forgetting as such things have long since lost any impact due to the commonality of such things. When you have a hundred people open up with fully automatic weapons at you, you stop paying attention to the individual bullets, even though any one of them could still kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:06:03-07:00","id":626960,"title":"","content":"I tend to be wary of politicians that present themselves as reformers - fast, drastic changes often bring significant problems with them - but I like Sanders okay.<br /> <br /> My only real concern is that if Hillary gets the nod, he doesn't Ralph-Nader the election for the left. I can't help having that concern about someone who styles himself an independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:28:27-07:00","id":626972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626473#post626473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I found out it's just one poll, but nonetheless, this guy looks....genuine.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is. He's just a long shot at this point regarding becoming the POTUS. If he wants, he's exceedingly well positioned to be a major contender for VP, and if not, he's still a Senator. He's not going anywhere in terms of being a player in US politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If, by some benevolent twist of history, he ends up as the Democratic candidate (or better yet, the POTUS), the US will have returned to the good old times when it was more progressive and radical than its European cousins. That is, if Bernie is allowed to implement his policies. </div> </div> </div>That last part is the important part though, especially in terms of US politics. US politics almost universally drive the president into being a centrist. They have to get things done, and it's a lot harder to get things done when you only going to push progressive laws. The conservatives need something in return, or you get gridlock, and then nothing gets done.<br /> <br /> Bernie's biggest weakness as a candidate is that he's such a staunch progressive. He runs a huge risk of getting into office, and then getting no Republican support for anything (keeping in mind that the Republicans control the Congress) put forward by a socialist (which is a very bad word in Republican circles), and getting nothing done.<br /> <br /> For all I'm on the progressive side of things, I do appreciate that the people in the country that have very different political ideals, and they deserve representation and consideration. The POTUS can't really operate well if they're seen as only representing the interests of half the country.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, Clinton scares me in a TTIP-TPP-TISA signing kind of way. </div> </div> </div>And that's the kind of argument Bernie's supporters should focus on. &quot;Hillary voted/would vote/etc. for X, Bernie would do Y.&quot; And fortunately, Bernie actually has specific plans for what he'd do about his main issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626719#post626719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People hear a name, recognise it, it fits into some shapes in their mind, and the contexts associated with that shape decide level of support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Though Bernie's at plenty of risk of that as well, because of the heavy baggage being a socialist in US politics carries; even if he doesn't have nearly the fame of Hillary in mainstream media. That said, if you're paying any attention to US presidential politics right now.... you know that Bernie Sanders is a person to pay attention to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are supporting a Bush, so he's probably going to be like that previous Bush and the Bush before him, or you're supporting a Kennedy, well he'll probably be like the other bits of the Kennedy family elected. </div> </div> </div>Which is true psychologically, but it gets to an interesting point. If you're voting for Jeb, are you voting for his father, or his brother? Because the Bushes were not easily comparable presidencies. You didn't get Bush Sr. part II with his son.<br /> <br /> It's also a fuzzy thing because Hillary, unlike the previous presidential &quot;dynasties&quot; isn't related to any previous presidents by blood. She's married to a former president. And long before she ran for public office herself (which she's been at for a bit), or married Bill, she was a very active political individual. Sure she mixes fame with being put in the Clinton box, but she's also done plenty with her career to say that she's not just Clinton part II (though Bill was a pretty well liked president). The political attacks on her so far are really interesting in that they like to use the &quot;Clinton = another Clinton&quot; thing, but really don't want to push the &quot;She'll be Clinton part II!&quot; because Bill is a very well liked president. So they switch it to Obama part II instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that makes some people uncomfortable since your leaders coming from largely family lines... well, it's that whole US and kings and lords thing. </div> </div> </div>Of course. There's a difference though, between being uncomfortable on a basic level, and then taking that discomfort and running with it without further examination and thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BS is doing exactly that right now. </div> </div> </div>He did stumble a bit on this compared to Hillary though. Hillary has not suffered blacklash from the Black Lives Matter movement, because she played that correctly from the get go. He's had to recover from a slip on it; despite it very impressive record on the subject.<br /> <br /> He's also got a big obstacle ahead of him in that Hillary's platform, and policies, are actually very similar to his own. Being seen as the outsider - which is a good narrative right now - is good for polls and crowds, but not necessarily for elections. It's really hard to get the nomination when it's, &quot;I've crafted a different public image with which to pass 95% the same laws,&quot; as your biggest selling point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626736#post626736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wanted to remind people that destruction of public records happened. I think people have forgotten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually we don't know if it even happened. None of the current investigations are really going there. The current issues being investigated are about the security of the server, and if classified documents were at risk because of it. Anything about the possible destruction of public records seems to be long dead as an issue.<br /> <br /> For all we know, she actually was very careful, and only deleted personal emails, and never deleted something that was required to be recorded. While historians love it when public officials leave behind personal stuff; they aren't under any obligation to (LBJ's phone calls to his tailor are awesome, but if he had erased them... who'd care?). Hilary's emails to Bill about dinner plans for Saturday aren't public records.<br /> <br /> And... what's the point of reminding people?<br /> <br /> Does it make Bernie a better candidate? Nope.<br /> <br /> Is it going to be an issue that sticks as it currently stands? Nope. The Clintons have a double-edged sword of often doing somewhat inane things, that turn into scandals very easily because they look bad, but are then very good at turning that around as nothing comes out of the scandals. Basically, in 6 months, this will be one of a number of attacks that will get thrown at Hillary, and nobody will care because it turned out to be another dud. Heck, I wouldn't be surprised if the Clintons kind of like tossing this sort of stuff in the mix because controversy they create is easier to manage to defuse, than controversy they didn't.<br /> <br /> Does it, in the actual big picture of history, and the future, matter? Maybe. But let's face it, lots of presidents have done far worse things before getting elected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:42:30-07:00","id":626985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626972#post626972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... what's the point of reminding people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The dull acceptance and passive endorsement of forgetfulness horrifies me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T15:37:05-07:00","id":627053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626985#post626985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dull acceptance and passive endorsement of forgetfulness horrifies me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a psychological defense mechanism. Humanity could not survive without it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T22:41:26-07:00","id":627279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626985#post626985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dull acceptance and passive endorsement of forgetfulness horrifies me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then... you're in for a pretty horrific life?<br /> <br /> Though really, this just reeks of general political tribalism. Anyone that might dislike your favored candidate, or like a different one more, could have only arrived at this position by doing some sort of negative thing that allows them to be othered.<br /> <br /> The assumption that people forgot (who exactly, demonstrated this behavior here?) serves no useful purpose.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T01:49:48-07:00","id":628381,"title":"","content":"Bernie Sanders is definitely a real candidate - he's filed the paperwork, and everything. The question is, just how viable a candidate is he?<br /> <br /> Right now, there's a lot of suspicion that his poll numbers are due primarily to the &quot;Anyone But Hillary&quot; camp. There's a sizable portion of the Democratic Party that's horrified at the idea of the Clintons back in the White House, either for their moderate/&quot;triangulating&quot; politics, or their (perceived) lack of ethics. In 2008, despite being a fresh candidate, with a powerful organization behind her, (then) Senator Hillary Clinton lost to both Barack Obama <i>and</i> John Edwards in Iowa (the first election of the '08 presidential campaign). In fact, its well-documented (if not widely known) that (then) Senator Obama was specifically recruited by the Democratic establishment to run against her. <br /> <br /> And there's a lot of suspicion that Senator Sanders is just picking up those same anti-Clinton votes. He isn't even a member of the Democratic Party - he's an independent who sides with them on organizational votes. And career-wise, he's best known as a &quot;talking head&quot; on cable news - a good source for a liberal quote, not so much for getting policy implemented.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean he can't win the Democratic nomination - he's setting record crowds, after all. But a lot of pundits still believe his poll numbers are &quot;soft&quot;, and liable to melt away if another viable anti-Hillary candidate gets into the race. No one's sure who that'd be (although there's a lot of talk about Vice President Biden jumping into the race), and the window to launch a successful campaign is closing fast . . . But the doubts are there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=626972#post626972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Which is true psychologically, but it gets to an interesting point. If you're voting for Jeb, are you voting for his father, or his brother? Because the Bushes were not easily comparable presidencies. You didn't get Bush Sr. part II with his son.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but between the two Bush presidencies, you cover much of the Republican establishment. George W. (Bush 43) went out of his way to pick advisors that disagreed with his father . . So it'll be hard for Jeb to find ones who think outside the &quot;Bush box&quot;. He'll be picking from a mix of ones who agreed with his father, or his brother, so he'd likely govern somewhere in between the two. <br /> <br /> (In theory, he could turn to the Tea Party . . . but the Bush family represents a lot of what the Tea Party dislikes about the Republican establishment)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also a fuzzy thing because Hillary, unlike the previous presidential &quot;dynasties&quot; isn't related to any previous presidents by blood. She's married to a former president. And long before she ran for public office herself (which she's been at for a bit), or married Bill, she was a very active political individual. Sure she mixes fame with being put in the Clinton box, but she's also done plenty with her career to say that she's not just Clinton part II (though Bill was a pretty well liked president). The political attacks on her so far are really interesting in that they like to use the &quot;Clinton = another Clinton&quot; thing, but really don't want to push the &quot;She'll be Clinton part II!&quot; because Bill is a very well liked president. So they switch it to Obama part II instead. </div> </div> </div>Well, with the Clintons, the slogan was always &quot;Two for the Price of One&quot; . . . and the Clintons have steadfastly refused to explain what role they see the former President taking, in a Hillary administration. Plus, much of the organization/machine she's using for her own run was originally built for his . . .<br /> <br /> And that's a large part of what's weirding people out about her run. Its almost like an American verison of Eva Perone . . . but with a still-living husband. <br /> <br /> But that's not the only issue with the Clintons. Sure, their policies were widely popular at the time <i>with the general public</i>. . . but a lot of that came only after their proposed healthcare reform (known at the time as &quot;Hillarycare&quot;) crashed and burned. And many in the liberal wing of the party never forgave them for their &quot;triangulation&quot; and move to more centrist policies in the aftermath. <br /> <br /> Plus, character-wise, a lot of people found them kind of sleazy. Questionable business dealings, Bill's philandering (Monica Lewinsky, a sexual harassment lawsuit, allegations of prostitutes . . .), quibbling over the meaning of &quot;is&quot; . . . And somehow, a lot of antique furniture from the White House &quot;accidentally&quot; got mixed in with theirs, when they moved out . . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually we don't know if it even happened. None of the current investigations are really going there. The current issues being investigated are about the security of the server, and if classified documents were at risk because of it. Anything about the possible destruction of public records seems to be long dead as an issue.<br /> <br /> For all we know, she actually was very careful, and only deleted personal emails, and never deleted something that was required to be recorded. While historians love it when public officials leave behind personal stuff; they aren't under any obligation to (LBJ's phone calls to his tailor are awesome, but if he had erased them... who'd care?). Hilary's emails to Bill about dinner plans for Saturday aren't public records. . . </div> </div> </div>Listening to the standards they used to decide which emails to hand over, and which to delete, I'd be surprised if some important/business/government emails weren't deleted by accident. Apparently they made the decision based on &quot;key word&quot; searches, without fully reviewing the emails in question. <br /> <br /> For example, Secretary Clinton keeps coming back to her yoga class (as an example of emails she's deleted). Assume they did a search and delete for emails containing the word &quot;yoga&quot;, yeah, you'd delete a lot of personal emails about how sore she was after class, and her new yoga outfit. But you also might delete emails where she had to skip her yoga lesson because of an important meeting, or an international crisis. <br /> <br /> On a side note - I've never heard the LBJ-tailor phone calls. Any recommendations on where I can find them? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T06:37:18-07:00","id":628489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=627279#post627279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then...you're in for a pretty horrific life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am, and have been. I wish you could have thought of a way to berate me for wanting to compare one political candidate's record to another's without needing to rub my face in how general of a failure as a human being I am, but<br /> <br /> Never mind. It's not worth it. You win, Heavy Arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T12:43:57-07:00","id":628968,"title":"","content":"I'm not &quot;berating&quot; you for wanting to compare candidates records.<br /> <br /> I'm &quot;berating&quot; you for thinking that shouting out random snippets of one side's record outside of their full context counts as comparison. If you actually want to run down the pros and cons of each, and why that makes Sanders the better in the end? That'd be awesome. I'd love to see that. But as One Vorlon pointed out, Sanders being the, &quot;I'm not Hillary&quot; candidate really doesn't seem like it amounts to much.<br /> <br /> If you just want to slam Hillary. You're not doing Bernie any favors, or the thread any favors. If you want to bitch about being called out on it? Less favors being done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T15:45:18-07:00","id":629127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=628968#post628968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to bitch about being called out on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I wanted to express that what you said really, really hurt my feelings. I expressed myself very badly because I let my fear of you stop me from just explicitly saying it and I instead rather childishly tried to bury the sentiment behind implications, and even now I can't force myself to explain exactly why that hurt so much because I don't trust you not to weaponize the information of why it's so intensely and personally painful to me, but there it is. That's all I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> I had hoped I would feel better for saying it. Oh well. You don't have to worry about me speaking up in this thread any more, Heavy Arms. As I said earlier, you win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T16:15:22-07:00","id":629158,"title":"","content":"From what I've been able to gather Bernie is viable but likely to lose against Hillary. My main reluctance on hos front, after extended conversations with one of my close friends whose an Economics major is that Bernie's economic policies are honestly just terrible. Not that the Republican ones are any better, and I'm in the dark on Hillary's so I can't comment there. As an Environmental Studies major from what I know he leans in the right direction in that department. But honestly at this point not only do I need to get more informed about the candidates as a whole I don't want to endorse someone due to one factor. I want someone who will be good for the nation as a whole whether or not I agree with them on every issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T18:25:49-07:00","id":629364,"title":"","content":"Bernie is an old-school Democrat who believes that the federal government is supposed to help the people of the country. There are some areas of his platform that I like, such as universal healthcare and free college tuition. I was less than impressed with the way he let the Black Lives Matter protesters walked all over him at those two rallies, though to be fair to him, he was basically stuck between a rock and a hardplace - bow to them and look weak or argue back and look like a racist.<br /> <br /> Realistically though, even if Bernie was elected, he probably wouldn't be able to get enough support from other Democrats to implement a lot of his policies, nevermind trying to pull in bipartisan support.<br /> <br /> If Bernie ends up as the democratic nominee, I'll vote for him. But if Hilary wins the nomination, then we'll see who the Republican candidate is. If it's Jeb and Hillary, then I'm going to have to hope that Trump is running as an independent, since I'd sooner vote for Trump than either of those two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T21:59:31-07:00","id":629552,"title":"","content":"Trump won't run as an independent, if he doesn't get the Republican nomination he'll bow out. I'd guess if he seems popular enough they'll go with him.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see if Bernie would be asked to be vice president, but who knows. I've only started looking into him since this thread but, as Okami points out, he's not very strong on understanding the economy. Of course that's hardly stopped anyone from becoming president.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2015, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T00:24:31-07:00","id":629638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Okami</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=629158#post629158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main reluctance on hos front, after extended conversations with one of my close friends whose an Economics major is that Bernie's economic policies are honestly just terrible. Not that the Republican ones are any better, and I'm in the dark on Hillary's so I can't comment there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Bernie gets a bit harshly slammed on the economic front. Most economists slam him... but he's also a socialist while the mainstream academic economist thought in American is staunchly market focused. If you're anti-socialist, socialist economic policies are going to be, by default, easy to bash of poorly thought out.<br /> <br /> If you look at him in depth, part of the problem is that he doesn't really have much in the ways of distinct specific policies; which is very easy to mistake for having bad policies. His specifics are actually pretty strong. If you look at his own 12 platform positions, some have much better defined concepts, and policies, and others are much more vague. A lot of the assessments of his economic policies are aimed more at those vague ones.<br /> <br /> Hillary's policies overlap a lot with Bernie. And are basically where Bernie's policies would end up if there was a Democratic supermajority where he'd have to negotiate down from his farther left starting point, but only with other Democrats. Which in many senses ends up meaning Hillary's economics come off as more sensible (though it is a bit odd in a political sense, if you consider that Bernie has more to &quot;give up&quot; in negotiations with conservatives than Hillary does in regards to getting a deal through a mix of power like we have now).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=629364#post629364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Bernie ends up as the democratic nominee, I'll vote for him. But if Hilary wins the nomination, then we'll see who the Republican candidate is. If it's Jeb and Hillary, then I'm going to have to hope that Trump is running as an independent, since I'd sooner vote for Trump than either of those two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to admit... I'm morbidly curious who in the Republican field you'd consider the optimal choice if you had to vote for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T08:02:08-07:00","id":629944,"title":"","content":"Last I heard Trump outright declared that if he doesn't get the nomination he'll run as an independent. Of course, the whole statements made during an election thing.<br /> <br /> As for economics... all I've really heard on Bernie is he's opposed to wide open borders for immigration, he wants to focus on raising the standard of living of americans rather than have open economic borders which encourages shifting jobs out of the country. and he's in favor of almost free higher education.<br /> <br /> Which... is not too bad of a platform honestly.<br /> <br /> Can someone expand and clear up the economic position/problems with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:02:46-07:00","id":629976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=629638#post629638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit... I'm morbidly curious who in the Republican field you'd consider the optimal choice if you had to vote for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Republican candidate I might be willing to vote for is Esteban Olivarez. He's pushing a heavily centrist platform, but he's quite a small fish compared to the other candidates, isn't a career politician, plus he's such a moderate - and Hispanic - that I don't think that there's any way he'd ever be able to make it through the primaries. But maybe in another 4 or 8 years he might be able to get up on the radar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-17-2015, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:11:11-07:00","id":629982,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that the parties are still picking candidates. There's a very old habit of candidates swinging widely to the outer edges to get the party support and then towards the middle in the general election.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T09:14:45-07:00","id":629983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=629944#post629944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last I heard Trump outright declared that if he doesn't get the nomination he'll run as an independent. Of course, the whole statements made during an election thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>He might have just said that to seem more serious about running, but if he has to go Independent he's going to have to shell out a lot of his own money for the campaign and I don't believe he's going to do that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T10:35:41-07:00","id":630024,"title":"","content":"He's already shelling out his own money, he frequently points that out. Watching MSNBC's coverage of Trump right now, have it on for background noise. As for Sanders, I'm seriously considering volunteering for his campaign, he's my preferred candidate by far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T14:18:44-07:00","id":630248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=630024#post630024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's already shelling out his own money, he frequently points that out. Watching MSNBC's coverage of Trump right now, have it on for background noise. As for Sanders, I'm seriously considering volunteering for his campaign, he's my preferred candidate by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but he's not running a full on campaign completely without the support of a party like he would if he had to go Independent. Plus there's a lot of little things you have to do to satisfy state requirements to get on the ballot as an Independent that he might not be able to fulfill.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly liking Sanders too, good on you if you volunteer for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-17-2015, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T23:55:56-07:00","id":630765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=628381#post628381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note - I've never heard the LBJ-tailor phone calls. Any recommendations on where I can find them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I realized I kind of skipped this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zNMo8kl7Ac\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zNMo8kl7Ac\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zNMo8kl7Ac\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zNMo8kl7Ac </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T03:07:20-07:00","id":638900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread#post625380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .As a European and a graduate of politics, I must say that the Bernie Sanders campaign has caught me by surprise. Is this for real? Is he honestly leading the poll for the Democrat presidential candidacy? What do American forum members think of him?<br /> <br /> (I ask this because my initial reaction to this guy is very positive)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're interested in following the presidential race, I recommend <b>RealClearPolitics</b> (<a href=\"http://www.realclearpolitics.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.realclearpolitics.com</a>). Every day, it posts links to the top ten-twenty political articles and editorials from major newspapers, all across the U.S. Their own in-house commentary tends to skew vaguely conservative, but they link to articles from the full political spectrum, from hard left to hard right.<br /> <br /> Even better, they post <i>all</i> the major polls, and even aggregate them into a Poll of Polls. Its a great way to keep track of who is up, and who is down. And even the major news networks (including CNN, NBCNews, and Fox) often refer to the RCP poll of polls in their own coverage. So the site's really a good one-stop-shop for American political news. They don't get everything . . . but they get a lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and pay particular attention to the polls in Iowa and New Hampshire. Each state and territory holds their own election (with their own rules), but the Iowa caucuses and the New Hampshire primary come well before the others, and the results there traditionally winnow the field down to three candidates or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 08-25-2015, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T03:22:14-07:00","id":638905,"title":"","content":"No one wants to talk about the candidacy of Deez Nutz?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T07:36:04-07:00","id":639086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=638905#post638905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one wants to talk about the candidacy of Deez Nutz?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly. Yes, it shows the willingness of the populace to embrace the silly, yes it shows the dissatisfaction of the people with the candidates offered, no it's not going to go anywhere if for no other reason than the kid is underage to run. <br /> <br /> The joke candidate(s) is also something that crops up in politics every so often, sometimes it catches attention like this and spreads.... admittedly I've not seen it as wide spread as this since the Vote Ficus thing back in the 90's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T12:36:57-07:00","id":639378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/625380-what-do-us-and-non-us-citizens-think-about-this-guy-politics-thread?p=638900#post638900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><u>Edit</u></i>: Oh, and pay particular attention to the polls in Iowa and New Hampshire. Each state and territory holds their own election (with their own rules), but the Iowa caucuses and the New Hampshire primary come well before the others, and the results there traditionally winnow the field down to three candidates or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth remembering though, that while Iowa and New Hampshire will probably reduce the field a bit, this could be an odd year. The changes in campaign finance laws have altered the necessity of doing well in the early States. In the past, doing poorly in the early votes usually meant funding drying up as financial backers jumped ship for more successful looking candidates. With the laws as they are, a lot of pundits are predicting less winnowing because more candidates are being backed by smaller numbers of extremely wealthy backers. Basically, it's easier to keep running because you've got someone gambling money they can afford to lose to keep you in.<br /> <br /> It's also important to keep in mind that winning these contests is not all that predictive (the numbers are highly skewed by incumbent candidates running unopposed). In the last six New Hampshire primaries, the eventual president only won 50% of the time. But when you unpack that, Clinton, Bush, and Obama all lost their first time in New Hampshire, and won their second time. A non-incumbent president hasn't won the New Hampshire primary since Bush Sr. in 1988. <br /> <br /> This is somewhat the mixed blessing of being the first. There's a lot of attention, and a lot of power in being first, but ultimately it's power is more because of how it impacts public perceptions for marginal candidates, not for how it predictive is contests will be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}